{
  "_readme": [
    "Tanglish helper for the classifier. Edit freely, then retrain (python trainer.py) and redeploy.",
    "All words are lowercase. Repeated letters are ignored when matching, so 'panuga' also covers 'panugaaa', 'pannugaa', 'ppanuga'.",
    "spellings: every listed spelling is treated as the same word (the key).",
    "tags: a word in a tag list adds a meaning signal the model learns once for the whole group.",
    "sense_rules: if the message contains one of these words, that anchor is read in its normal meaning and skipped (e.g. pvt + company).",
    "self_words / request_words: next to an anchor, these mean it IS a DM ask, so the sense rule does not apply (add me, pvt vaa).",
    "REQUEST covers 'do it / send it / come / let's talk' words: in this group 'pm vaa' and 'pm pannunga' mean the same thing.",
    "cant_words: 'can't / didn't see / not coming / don't understand' (msg panna mudiyala, en txt pakkala, msg varala). A DM word next to one of these is skipped as a complaint, UNLESS the message also has a request_verbs word ('group la pesa mudiyala dm pannunga' is still a DM ask).",
    "group_words: a msg/message/text word right next to one of these ('group la msg pannuga', 'inga msg pannu', 'text here') means send it IN THE GROUP, which is allowed. Cancelled if the message has any private_words word.",
    "sense_rules for msg/message/text/txt/mes: words that mean 'a message in the group' (msg dltd, voice msg pin, repeated msg, msg kanom, reaction).",
    "PAST also covers 'did / didn't / is doing / they are doing' forms (msg pannala, msg pannirnga, msg pandrom, msg panraanga): describing a message, not asking for one.",
    "topic_words: if the replied-to message or the last 10 messages (5 min) from others use one of these or any DM word, the conversation is about messaging, so a can't/didn't reply ('Msg panna mudiyala' to 'un msg ye kaanom') is allowed. Out of the blue, it's checked like any other message.",
    "neg_before / neg_after: a DM word right after a neg_before word ('don't pm me', 'no dm') or followed within 2 words by a neg_after word ('dm pannathinga', 'pm vendam') is a refusal or a rule, not a request, unless the message also has a request verb.",
    "reported_after: a DM word followed within 3 words by one of these describes what SOMEONE ELSE did ('antha ponnu enaku dm pannuchu', 'private msg panraanga'), a report, not a request.",
    "sense_rules add: adding to a group/channel ('whatsapp group la add pannunga'); contact: business contact ('cake order venumna contact pannunga').",
    "asking_around: an ask word + a target word + a here/for-friendship word ('Any girls here', 'Any akka irukingala', 'Any ladies for friendship') is asking around for women: .delwarn 'no dating txt'. If the message also asks for DM, the DM mute wins."
  ],
